WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.762
Runbook R oh two's first step sets out
the rights each depth of discovery needs.

2
00:00:04.762 --> 00:00:09.613
Read access to Active Directory finds
candidates; it doesn't complete the inventory.

3
00:00:09.613 --> 00:00:14.695
The directory depth gives candidate hosts
and instances from S P Ns and directory

4
00:00:14.695 --> 00:00:16.639
objects, and needs nothing more:

5
00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:20.226
the SQL Server Browser probe
needs only a network path.

6
00:00:20.226 --> 00:00:24.316
The host depth gives the instances
installed and each service's account,

7
00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:28.612
and needs local administrator by default,
or a least-privilege alternative.

8
00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:32.968
The instance depth gives the version,
the mode, every login and the databases,

9
00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:36.563
and needs a Windows login with
the Start Kit's read permissions.

10
00:00:36.563 --> 00:00:37.812
Never sysadmin.

11
00:00:37.812 --> 00:00:40.325
Azure Arc is an optional fourth depth.

12
00:00:40.325 --> 00:00:44.228
Run every depth under one dedicated
discovery identity per forest,

13
00:00:44.228 --> 00:00:48.897
a group managed service account for
scheduled runs, and add the host and instance

14
00:00:48.897 --> 00:00:53.300
rights for the assessment window only,
recording each grant and its removal.
